course: dictionary
lesson: 4239
title: Family words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: You can learn a word from the sentence around it. «At the front walks the grandmother, who remembers where the water is and which dangers to avoid.» Remembers where the water is and knows the dangers tells you she has lived a long time, so grandmother is a family member who is old and wise.
explain: Stories and nature use the same word. «Orca groups are led by old grandmothers who remember where salmon are in bad years.» The clue old, and the fact that she leads, tells you a grandmother can be the oldest, most experienced female in a family.
explain: Some words in a family have different names for the same person. «Grandma», «Granny», «Nan» and «Nana» are all everyday names for a grandmother, so when you read one of them, you can work out who the story means.
fact: Grandmother is a noun. Its plural is grandmothers.
fact: A grandmother is the mother of your mother or of your father.
fact: Children often call her Grandma, Granny, Nan or Nana.
fact: A great-grandmother is the mother of your grandmother or grandfather.
fact: «Grandmother» appears in stories too, such as Little Red Riding Hood's grandmother.
exercise: «At the front walks the grandmother, the matriarch.» In the elephant herd, who walks at the front? | A visitor from the zoo | The youngest aunt | The smallest baby | *The grandmother
exercise: Grandma, Granny, Nan and Nana are all names a child might use for whom? | *Your grandmother | Your great-grandfather | Your teacher | Your cousin
exercise: «Orca groups are led by old grandmothers.» Which word tells you the grandmothers have lived a long time? | led | *old | orca | groups
test: A great-grandmother is the mother of whom? | Your cousin | Your teacher | Your sister | *Your grandmother or grandfather
test: Which name might a child use for her grandmother? | Sister | Niece | Cousin | *Nana
exam: Mia says a grandmother is the mother of your teacher. Is she right? | *No, she is the mother of your mother or of your father | Yes, it is another word for a cousin | No, it is a word for a sister | Yes, every teacher has one
